BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trans Collective Library : Opening and Donation Drive
UID:evenement9080 @ http://www.resistancemontreal.org
DTSTAMP:20260809T150754Z
DTSTART:20260817T190000Z
DTEND:20260817T170300Z
CREATED:20260809T150754Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T150754Z 
LOCATION:Galerie l'articule, 6282 St-Hubert (métro Beaubien) 
DESCRIPTION:We are thrilled to announce our reading room and collective library\, running Monday\, August 17th – Sunday\, August 30 at articule. We are setting up a reading room and collective library in articule’s space to showcase trans literature\, essays\, art\, zines\, and other printed materials. All are invited to donate or lend printed materials that address trans lives\, desires\, fantasies\, politics\, advocacy\, erotics\, and other facets of trans experience. Dick’s entire collection will also be available for browsing\, including our non-circulating (more rare and precious) titles. See below for more details. ✨ Opening ✨ Monday\, August 17\, 3:00-7:00 Come by during our opening event to lend or donate books\, zines\, printed essays\, and other print materials to the collective library for the duration of the reading room. We are looking for : Materials written/created by trans\, non-binary\, or Two Spirit people Materials written/created by gender non-conforming authors who self-identify in other ways Materials that relate to trans issues and experiences more broadly Materials that we don’t already carry in our collection (see our catalogue) Or just come by to say hi and/or learn about how to get involved with the library ! 📚 Librarian hours 📚 Mondays\, Wednesdays\, Fridays\, Sundays\, 12-6pm Visit us during our librarian hours to drop off additional donations or loans to the reading room\, peruse the collective library\, hang & read some books or zines\, and chat about the library. 🎈 Closing Event 🎈 Sunday\, Aug. 30 (closing event\, time TBA) Join us for a reading and fundraiser for Metonymy Press to close the reading room and celebrate the re-launch of our lending services. More info coming soon ! 💖 Access Info 💖 articule (6282 Rue St-Hubert) is wheelchair-accessible and has one gender neutral washroom K/N95 masks provided at all times K/N95 masks required for opening and closing events A HEPA filter air purifier will be in the space Fragrance-free. Please refrain from wearing any perfume or scented items.
CATEGORIES:événements
URL:https://www.resistancemontreal.org/calendrier/article/evenements?id_evenement=9080

