s part of our anticolonial commitment to opposing occupation\, apartheid\, and state violence. We refuse to let queer identity be used to sanitize oppression. Community Solidarity means showing up for one another materially\, emotionally\, and politically\, especially for Black\, Indigenous\, and racialized communities who face the harshest impacts of oppression. Our liberation is collective\, never individual. Community Care Community care is how we survive in a world that isolates us. We share labor\, resources\, and emotional support so our communities can rest\, heal\, and thrive. Liberation of Oppressed Peoples We align ourselves with communities worldwide resisting imperialism\, extraction\, and militarized violence. Queer liberation is bound up with global struggles for land\, safety\, dignity\, and self‑determination. Prison abolition We hate the police and prisons as much as you do ! 🙂 Pro‑Palestine Wild Pride stands with Palestinians resisting occupation\, apartheid\, and genocide. Our solidarity rejects pinkwashing and affirms that queer liberation is inseparable from global anticolonial struggle. Queer and trans Joy Queer and trans joy is a form of resistance that honors our beauty\, creativity\, and survival. Joy reminds us that liberation is not only struggle\, but celebration. Transformative Justice We address harm through repair\, accountability\, and community support rather than punishment or policing. Transformative justice helps us build structures that prevent harm and strengthen our relationships. Transparency Transparency prevents hierarchy\, ego politics\, and hidden power. We share decisions\, budgets\, and timelines openly so our community can trust the process and participate fully.
CATEGORIES:événements
URL:https://www.resistancemontreal.org/calendrier/article/evenements?id_evenement=9026

